<speak>A separate tray sounds sensible. At present there is a tray marked for me, but everyone treats it as a place for anything they do not know where to put. I have found a supplier catalogue, a birthday card, and a spare set of meeting-room keys in there together. Maybe the label needs to say personal correspondence rather than just my name. I prefer to review banking correspondence privately, not while somebody is standing in the doorway waiting for a signature. Even if the letter is routine, I want the habit to be the same. Otherwise exceptions become the usual arrangement very quickly.</speak>